  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large clay pot over medium heat.",
    "Add the onion and cook until softened, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the garlic, ginger, and Ras el hanout, and cook for 1 minute, stirring constantly.",
    "Add the chicken and cook until browned on all sides, about 5-7 minutes.",
    "Add the chicken broth, pitted dates, paprika, salt, and black pepper.",
    "Stir to combine, then bring the mixture to a boil.",
    "Reduce the heat to low and simmer, covered, for 25-30 minutes, or until the chicken is cooked through.",
    "Stir in the chopped almonds and cook for an additional 2 minutes.",
    "Serve the tagine hot, garnished with chopped fresh cilantro.",
    "Let the tagine rest for 10 minutes before serving, allowing the flavors to meld together."
